ry Office of Study Abroad Registrar Student Counseling Services Student Government Association Student Handbook Student Health Services Student Success and Student Life Testing Services The Writing and Reading Center Tutoring Resources Veteran Services Student Life Student Life Bookstore Catalog Dateline Downtown Dean of Students Events Calendar eSports Gator Resource Center iRadio Sports & Fitness Student Leadership & Involvement Student Organizations Student Success and Student Life Connect with us today! For Students For Students For Students Previous Next UHD / Student Success and Student Life / Student Success Initiatives / Center for Career and Professional Development UHD Center for Career and Professional Development Navigate This Section UHD Center for Career and Professional Development About Us Mission and Vision Staff Hours and Location Employers How to Get Involved on Campus Internships Micro-internships Virtual Career Fair Resources for Employers Career Assessment Career Readiness Explore Majors & Careers Majors and Careers Financial Information Students' Career Outcomes Job/Internship Search Strategies Internship Career/Job Volunteer Résumé/CV & Cover Letters Interview Graduate School Starting a Business Faculty Resources Frequent Asked Questions Contact Us UHD Center for Career and Professional Development One Main Street, S402 Houston, TX 77002 Office: 713-221-8980 [email protected] Office Hours Monday - Friday: 8am - 5pm Marilyn Davies College of Business: Same as above except for Wednesday: 8am - 7pm. Drop-In Hours (In-person & Virtual) *: Monday, 11am & 3pm Tuesday 9am & 3pm Wednesday, 1pm & 6pm (MDCOB office only) Thursday, 2pm & 3pm Friday, 10am & 3pm (*6:00 p.m. drop-in hours are available during the fall and spring long semesters\n                        only. During summer sessions and term breaks, the 6:00 p.m. drop-in time will shift\n                        to 3:00 p.m.) UHD CCPD Zoom Room | 143774 NOTE: Drop-ins are a quick 10-15 minute session and NOT an appointment. Appointments available in person, via telephone, or via Zoom. The UHD Center for Career and Professional Development (CCPD) is on this page to enhance\n                              the career development of students in the: College of Humanities and Social Sciences College of Public Service College of Sciences and Technology Marilyn Davies College of Business UHD Alumni UHD Center for Career and Professional Development Services Overview Career Planning: Assists students and alumni to know and understand themselves and the world of work\n                              in order to make career, educational, and life decisions. Self-Assessment: Students and alumni can complete formal self-assessments to identify personality characteristics,\n                              interests, and values related to their career of interest. For more information, please\n                              visit our self-assessment page. Gators4Hire Career System & Online Job Board: Upload resumes/cover letters for review by our Professional Development Specialists Conduct job searches and browse employer listings Make appointments with your Professional Development Specialist Engage in mock interviews RSVP for employer events and workshops Activate your Gators4Hire account . Résumé/CV & Cover Letter Writing: Our center assists students and alumni with basic and advanced professional writing.\n                              Print resources are available in our office outlining steps to create these professional\n                              documents. Electronic resources are also available on the Résumé - Application Preparations page. Graduate School Applications: Our Professional Development Specialists aid students in completing graduate school\n                              applications. Deadlines for applications are generally submitted one semester prior\n                              to admission. Get started early! Interview Preparation: Schedule a mock interview to prepare for the real thing, perfect your professionalism\n                              and work out your nerves. Our Professional Development Specialists conduct a tailored\n                              mock interview and provide quality feedback to students and alumni. For more information,\n                              visit the Interview - Application Preparations page. Must be scheduled one week in advance! Job/Internship Search: Looking for employment? Check out our online resources or talk with a Professional Development Specialist about search strategies. Networking Advice: Learn how to make and maintain contacts in your field. Find out more about events\n                              to practice your skills. If you have any questions, please call the UHD Center for Career and Professional Development at 713-221-8980 or send us an email at [email protected] Have no idea what you want to do after graduation? Already have a plan in place? We\n                              want to support you in your journey - in-person and virtually. Activate your Gators4Hire account to: • Make appointments with your Professional Development Specialist • Upload resumes/cover letters for review • Engage in mock interviews • Conduct job searches • RSVP for employer events and workshops ​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​​ Students/Alumni Login Employer Login Connect with us! YouTube ​ Instagram ​ LinkedIn Facebook One Main Street Houston, TX 77002 713-221-8000 Visitor Parking & Ride Share 201 Girard Street Houston, TX 77002 A–Z Index Academic Affairs Accessible Education Center Accreditation Campus Carry Policy Canvas Compact with Texans Directory Human Resources Information Technology Library Mental Health Resources Parking & Transportation Services Quality Enhancement Plan Student Achievement © 2026 University of Houston-Downtown Report a problem with this page University of Houston System Privacy Notice Fraud Reporting Fraud & Non-Compliance Hotline Linking Notice