Student Counseling Services Student Government Association Student Handbook Student Health Services Student Success and Student Life Testing Services The Writing and Reading Center Tutoring Resources Veteran Services Student Life Student Life Bookstore Catalog Dateline Downtown Dean of Students Events Calendar eSports Gator Resource Center iRadio Sports & Fitness Student Leadership & Involvement Student Organizations Student Success and Student Life At UHD ... Work alongside like-minded and highly talented professionals. At UHD ... Take advantage of our easy access downtown location. At UHD ... Expand professionally in an engaging higher education setting. At UHD ... Make a difference in the lives of our students. At UHD ... Join our commitment to the Houston community. At UHD ... Enjoy extensive benefits not offered by other employers. At UHD ... Participate in a fun work environment. Previous Next Faculty Staff Student/Temporary Employment UHD / Human Resources / Careers at UHD Careers at UHD Navigate This Section HR Home Careers at UHD Student Employment Temporary Employment Veteran's Preference Former Foster Preference Benefits Contact Us Telephone: 713-221-8060 [email protected] Tamika Small Manager, Talent Acquisition Telephone: 713-222-5318 [email protected] Cecealia Burns Coordinator, Student Employment Telephone: 713-223-7954 [email protected] Title IX/Equal Opportunity Office Brandon W. Lee Title IX/Equal Opportunity Officer 713-221-5771 [email protected] One Main Street, Suite S370 Houston, TX 77002 Join an engaged community dedicated to student success. Join UHD. We’re not just hiring employees—we’re building a community of people who want to create,\n                           innovate, and lead. At UHD, your ideas matter, your growth is supported, and your\n                           work makes a difference. Whether you’re just starting your career or bringing years of experience, you’ll find\n                           opportunities here to grow, contribute, and do meaningful work. Explore our open roles\n                           and discover how you can help shape the future. Employment at UHD Fulfilling UHD's mission to nurture talent, generate knowledge, and drive socioeconomic\n                                    mobility for a strong and sustainable future starts with you. We believe meaningful\n                                    work happens when talented people are empowered to think boldly, collaborate openly,\n                                    and grow continuously. We care deeply about the impact of our work—and the people\n                                    behind it. A core principle of the university is that learning extends far beyond the classroom—and\n                                    that belief shapes our approach to professional growth. We invest in continuous development\n                                    through a wide range of opportunities designed to support both technical and interpersonal\n                                    skills. The HR Talent Development team offers training focused on collaboration and\n                                    communication in the workplace. In addition, the Leadership Academy brings together\n                                    staff and faculty with demonstrated leadership potential for immersive learning experiences,\n                                    hands-on assignments, and workshops that strengthen their ability to lead with confidence\n                                    and impact. If you’re looking for a place where you can do purposeful work, learn every day, and\n                                    shape the lives of our students and the future, you’ll feel at home here. Our University Benefits Benefits We recognize that Work-Life balance is crucial for employees to sustain high-level\n                                    performance. We offer a comprehensive array of benefits designed to support your work,\n                                    well-being, and long-term growth. Our benefits include: Health, dental, and vision coverage , as well as a life, gap, and disability insurance A robust variety of retirement savings opportunities as a State of Texas institution Access to our free EAP platform, AllOne Health Free financial advising through our partner YourMoneyLine Unique discounts with businesses across Houston The opportunity to receive UHD class reimbursement when working toward a degree relevant to your role We’re always evolving our benefits offerings to meet the needs of our community—because\n                                    well-being is essential to doing great work. Our Community At UHD, community is at the heart of the employee experience. We believe recognition,\n                                    connection, and shared purpose are essential to a thriving workplace—and we create\n                                    meaningful opportunities for employees to engage with one another throughout the year. We celebrate excellence through ongoing recognition and signature events. Programs\n                                    like Kudos, our peer recognition system, allow employees to acknowledge colleagues\n                                    who go above and beyond, while our annual Staff Awards ceremony formally honors individuals\n                                    who demonstrate outstanding commitment and impact. Beyond recognition, our campus is enriched by traditions that bring people together.\n                                    From our longstanding President's Lecture Series and the College of Public Services' vitalvoices forum to the annual Chili Cook-Off and Tail-Gatoring , there are countless ways to connect with colleagues and participate in campus life. We also value shared governance and inclusive decision-making. Employees have opportunities\n                                    to contribute to institutional policies and priorities through established processes\n                                    and through active organizations such as the Faculty Council , Staff Council , and the Student Government Association . We encourage you to explore these groups and learn how many voices help shape UHD's\n                                    direction. Events The Talent Acquisition Department at UHD is dedicated to the recruitment and retention\n                           of qualified individuals. The University of Houston-Downtown is an Equal Opportunity\n                           employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, race, color, disability, religion,\n                           national origin, veteran’s status, genetic information, or sex (including pregnancy),\n                           sexual orientation, gender identity or status, or gender expression, except where\n                           such a distinction is required by law. Should you have any questions, please feel\n                           free to contact us . Thank you for your interest in UHD. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act of 2008, if accommodations\n                           are needed to complete the application process, please contact the Talent Acquisition\n                           team at 713-221-8060. Labor Compliance Notices Campus Security Report Each year, the University of Houston-Downtown publishes the UHD Annual Crime Report.\n                           It contains crime statistics for the three most recent calendar years. It also details\n                           UHD's security policies and procedures and identifies who on campus maintains information\n                           about registered criminal sexual offenders. The report is provided in accordance with\n                           the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics\n                           Act and is available online at UHD Annual Security Reports . To request a printed copy of the Annual Crime Report, call Police Records at 713-221-8065. See room for improvement? Fill out this HR Website Feedback Form to provide input. One Main Street Houston, TX 77002 713-221-8000 Visitor Parking & Ride Share 201 Girard Street Houston, TX 77002 A–Z Index Academic Affairs Accessible Education Center Accreditation Campus Carry Policy Canvas Compact with Texans Directory Human Resources Information Technology Library Mental Health Resources Parking & Transportation Services Quality Enhancement Plan Student Achievement © 2026 University of Houston-Downtown Report a problem with this page University of Houston System Privacy Notice Fraud Reporting Fraud & Non-Compliance Hotline Linking Notice Open Records Institutional Resume State Required Reports Texas Homeland Security Texas Public Information Act (TPIA) Texas.gov HB 2504 TRAIL Sexual Misconduct & Discrimination Reporting University Policies Texas Veterans Portal Student Issue or Concern Report ©"
    },
